From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: permission: auto-approve writes only where their path points

Build mode pre-approves Write/Edit into <cwd>/.zcode/workflow-drafts/,
accept-edits mode every Write/Edit and agent memory every .md write under
its root, all by path string. A repository can commit
.zcode/workflow-drafts -> ../.git (the next auto-approved git status runs
its core.fsmonitor) or a symlinked .zcode/agent-memory, and Bash can move
the working directory into .git.

The target must now stay inside the workspace root (agent memory: inside
its memory root), outside any .git directory in any letter case (.GIT is
.git on a case-folding filesystem), with no symlink on the way, and a
project or local agent memory root reached through a symlink is not used.
Any other write asks.

Patch-mainline: No

